            "id": "4946357",
            "title": "CLOA: AAA-Rated CLO Strategy For Risk-Taking Investors",
            "description": "<html><body><p data-eci=\"true\"><figure class=\"getty-figure\" data-type=\"getty-image\"><picture> <img alt=\"Living paycheck to paycheck. Work while there is payment. Investments and grants. Consumption of financial resources. Constant infusions of money. Endless lending and the inability to pay off debts.\" data-id=\"2188840610\" data-type=\"getty-image\" fetchpriority=\"high\" height=\"966\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) calc(100vw - 36px), (max-width: 1023px) calc(100vw - 132px), (max-width: 1199px) calc(100vw - 666px), (max-width: 1307px) calc(100vw - 708px), 600px\" src=\"https://static.seekingalpha.com/cdn/s3/uploads/getty_images/2188840610/image_2188840610.jpg?io=getty-c-w630\" srcset=\"https://static.seekingalpha.com/cdn/s3/uploads/getty_images/2188840610/image_2188840610.jpg?io=getty-c-w1536 1536w, https://static.seekingalpha.com/cdn/s3/uploads/getty_images/2188840610/image_2188840610.jpg?io=getty-c-w1280 1280w, https://static.seekingalpha.com/cdn/s3/uploads/getty_images/2188840610/image_2188840610.jpg?io=getty-c-w1080 1080w, https://static.seekingalpha.com/cdn/s3/uploads/getty_images/2188840610/image_2188840610.jpg?io=getty-c-w750 750w, https://static.seekingalpha.com/cdn/s3/uploads/getty_images/2188840610/image_2188840610.jpg?io=getty-c-w640 640w, https://static.seekingalpha.com/cdn/s3/uploads/getty_images/2188840610/image_2188840610.jpg?io=getty-c-w480 480w, https://static.seekingalpha.com/cdn/s3/uploads/getty_images/2188840610/image_2188840610.jpg?io=getty-c-w320 320w, https://static.seekingalpha.com/cdn/s3/uploads/getty_images/2188840610/image_2188840610.jpg?io=getty-c-w240 240w\" width=\"1536\"/> </picture><figcaption><p class=\"item-caption\"> </p> <p class=\"item-credits\">Andrii Yalanskyi/iStock via Getty Images</p></figcaption></figure></p> <p>The iShares AAA CLO Active ETF (<span class=\"ticker-hover-wrapper\"><a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/CLOA\" title=\"iShares AAA CLO Active ETF\">CLOA</a></span>) is an actively managed exchange-traded fund designed to provide investors with diversified exposure to the AAA-rated collateralized loan obligation [CLO] market. The fund effectively provides investors with access to the private credit market, providing broadly diversified exposure to the loans that make up the CLO portfolio. While CLOs are made up of a series of loans that are unrated or below investment grade, the portfolio that makes up each CLO generally diversifies credit risk, limiting exposure to any single issuer, allowing the CLOs to hold a high credit rating. CLOA can be best utilized as a component of a fixed income portfolio strategy by those seeking to diversify risk exposure.</p> <h3>About iShares AAA CLO Active ETF</h3> <p>CLOA <a href=\"http://www.ishares.com/us/products/330488/ishares-aaa-clo-active-etf\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\">was launched</a> on January 10, 2023 on the NASDAQ Exchange. The ETF currently has approximately $2.28 billion in net assets with an average of $21 million in share value changing hands on a daily basis, providing investors with significant trading depth for a 30-day median bid/ask spread of 0.02%. CLOA has an expense ratio of 20bps, aligned with peer AAA-rated CLO portfolio strategies.</p> <p><figure class=\"regular-img-figure\" contenteditable=\"false\"><picture> <span><a aria-label=\"Expand image into lightbox view\" data-height=\"237\" data-og-image-facebook=\"false\" data-og-image-google_news=\"false\" data-og-image-google_plus=\"false\" data-og-image-linkedin=\"false\" data-og-image-msn=\"false\" data-og-image-twitter_image_post=\"false\" data-og-image-twitter_large_card=\"false\" data-og-image-twitter_small_card=\"false\" data-width=\"1011\" href=\"https://static.seekingalpha.com/uploads/2026/9/12/16009792-17892396017197652_origin.png\" rel=\"lightbox\" role=\"button\"><img alt=\"Seeking Alpha\" contenteditable=\"false\" height=\"150\" loading=\"lazy\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) calc(100vw - 36px), (max-width: 1023px) calc(100vw - 180px), 552px\" src=\"https://static.seekingalpha.com/uploads/2026/9/12/16009792-17892396017197652_origin.png?io=w640\" srcset=\"https://static.seekingalpha.com/uploads/2026/9/12/16009792-17892396017197652_origin.png?io=w640 640w,https://static.seekingalpha.com/uploads/2026/9/12/16009792-17892396017197652_origin.png?io=w480 480w,https://static.seekingalpha.com/uploads/2026/9/12/16009792-17892396017197652_origin.png?io=w320 320w,https://static.seekingalpha.com/uploads/2026/9/12/16009792-17892396017197652_origin.png?io=w240 240w\" width=\"640\"/></a></span> </picture><figcaption><p class=\"item-caption\"><span>Seeking Alpha</span></p></figcaption></figure></p> <p>CLOA pays out a monthly distribution, most of which is attributed to investment income. The ETF paid out $2.50/share over the last twelve months for a yield of 4.82%. Given that distributions are a factor of cash flows earned by investing in CLOs, investors may be exposed to interest rate risk.</p> <p><figure class=\"regular-img-figure\" contenteditable=\"false\"><picture> <span><a aria-label=\"Expand image into lightbox view\" data-height=\"450\" data-og-image-facebook=\"true\" data-og-image-google_news=\"true\" data-og-image-google_plus=\"true\" data-og-image-linkedin=\"true\" data-og-image-msn=\"true\" data-og-image-twitter_image_post=\"true\" data-og-image-twitter_large_card=\"true\" data-og-image-twitter_small_card=\"true\" data-width=\"1300\" href=\"https://static.seekingalpha.com/uploads/2026/9/12/16009792-1789239601771393_origin.png\" rel=\"lightbox\" role=\"button\"><img alt=\"Seeking Alpha\" contenteditable=\"false\" height=\"222\" loading=\"lazy\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) calc(100vw - 36px), (max-width: 1023px) calc(100vw - 180px), 552px\" src=\"https://static.seekingalpha.com/uploads/2026/9/12/16009792-1789239601771393_origin.png?io=w640\" srcset=\"https://static.seekingalpha.com/uploads/2026/9/12/16009792-1789239601771393_origin.png?io=w640 640w,https://static.seekingalpha.com/uploads/2026/9/12/16009792-1789239601771393_origin.png?io=w480 480w,https://static.seekingalpha.com/uploads/2026/9/12/16009792-1789239601771393_origin.png?io=w320 320w,https://static.seekingalpha.com/uploads/2026/9/12/16009792-1789239601771393_origin.png?io=w240 240w\" width=\"640\"/></a></span> </picture><figcaption><p class=\"item-caption\"><span>Seeking Alpha</span></p></figcaption></figure></p> <p>Notably, CLOA’s portfolio is made up of mostly floating-rate CLOs and may invest upwards of 10% of net assets in fixed-rate CLOs. This means that CLOA’s value and cash flows will be tied to the Federal Reserve’s interest rate policy. In general, loans are priced at a spread on top of the secured overnight financing rate [SOFR], depending on the company’s risk profile. The payments and value of floating-rate notes will fluctuate with respect to interest rate policy; a rate hike will increase the value of the loan due to the higher rate whereas a rate cut will reduce the value and cash flow of the loan. In short, investors should consider floating-rate issuances during an interest rate tightening cycle and fixed-rate issuances as interest rate policy loosens.</p> <p>One value that CLOA can bring to an investor’s fixed income portfolio is its low effective duration rate of 0.12 years. This means that for a 1% change in the Federal Funds rate, CLOA can be expected to experience a 0.12% change in value. Similar to managing one’s total credit risk profile in their portfolio, CLOA can be used to manage their total portfolio’s duration risk. Depending on the investor’s perception of the market, lower duration risk can be beneficial during a rate tightening cycle as the value of fixed-rate issuances tend to have an inverse relationship with the Federal Funds rate, meaning that a rate hike will reduce the value of the fixed-rate portfolio. With floating-rate issuances having the opposite effect, CLOA can effectively limit interest rate exposure when applied to a fixed income portfolio strategy.</p> <h3>Investor Suitability</h3> <p>CLOA can be used by a variety of investors seeking to manage credit and duration risk. With the majority of the strategy being made up of floating-rate CLOs, CLOA can be strategically applied when going into a rate-tightening cycle. CLOA should not be considered as a complete portfolio solution, but rather, a component of a diversified fixed income portfolio. Investors may structure their portfolios using a diversified core portfolio strategy like the iShares Core US Aggregate Bond ETF (<a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/AGG\" title=\"iShares Core US Aggregate Bond ETF\">AGG</a>) to capture broad exposure across the US investment-grade bond market, adding satellite positions to diversify credit and duration risk in order to capture higher-yielding assets.</p> <p>CLOA can also be utilized for strategic positioning going into a rate-tightening cycle. While the debt markets aren’t as dynamic as the equities markets, CLOA can earn additional yield delivered by its floating rate.</p> <h3>Risks Related to CLOA</h3> <p>CLOA is an actively managed fixed income strategy designed to provide broad exposure to the AAA-rated CLO market, presenting certain risks that should be considered prior to making a final investment decision. CLOA will have direct exposure to interest rate risk given that the portfolio is primarily made up of floating-rate issuances. This means that the value and cash flows will be aligned with changes in the key interest rate set by the Federal Reserve, both increasing during rate hike cycles and decreasing during easing cycles.</p> <p>CLOs are made up of a portfolio of private loans, which may be considered high-yield and unrated, presenting significant credit risk despite the CLOs being rated AAA. While CLOA is made up of the highest rated CLOs, the securities aren’t insulated from losses and default risk during stressed market conditions. Events like rating downgrades, forced liquidation of the CLO, or the market’s anticipation of defaults can significantly influence the value of the securities.</p> <p>Investors will face manager risk for both CLOA and the CLOs themselves. The CLO manager is responsible for selecting, packing, and maintaining the loan obligations within the CLO portfolio. The portfolio management team is responsible for evaluating the CLO managers and actively selecting the appropriate CLOs to include in the portfolio.</p> <h3>Final Thoughts</h3> <p>Overall, CLOA can be used to earn monthly income, diversify credit exposure, and manage duration risk. CLOA’s portfolio of AAA-rated CLOs is made up of private loans that retail investors may otherwise not have access to. While CLOs inherently exhibit greater risk relative to the bond market, the underlying portfolios of loans can provide differentiated risk and returns with respect to the broader bond market.</p> <p>This article answers three questions about CLOA:</p> <ol> <li>What kind of holdings does CLOA have?</li> <li>What impacts CLOA's performance?</li> <li>Which investors is CLOA most suitable for?</li> </ol> <p><span><em>Editor's note:</em></span><em> This article is intended to provide a general overview of the ETF for educational purposes only and, unlike other articles on Seeking Alpha, does not offer an investment opinion about the ETF.</em></p></body></html>",
